--- BAS-07, 09, 10: comment placement, standalone position ---
a number called cupboard is 0.
Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.
Set cupboard to cupboard add 1. (workbench, checked)
If cupboard is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-07: expected 2 got {cupboard}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.

--- the same leaf, a seed that draws the trailing position ---
a number called 'the inbox' is 0.
Set 'the inbox' to 'the inbox' add 1.
Set 'the inbox' to 'the inbox' add 1. (see the sketchpad for details)
If 'the inbox' is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-07: expected 2 got {'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox'.

--- BAS-11: comment mid-declaration ---
a number (see the dispatch note for details) called 'the mailbag' is 578.
If 'the mailbag' is not 578 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-11: expected 578 got {'the mailbag'}", Exit 95. Print 'the mailbag'.

--- the same leaf, mid-expression ---
a number called 'the dispatch note' is 2030837 (nothing unusual here, just ledger) add 2147483648.
a number called 'the drawer' is 2030837 add 2147483648.
If 'the dispatch note' is not 'the drawer' then, Print "ASSERT BAS-11: expected {'the drawer'} got {'the dispatch note'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.

--- the same leaf, mid-condition ---
a number called 'the sketchpad' is 0.
If 8277419968124 (a note about the message slip) is greater than or equal to 0 then, Set 'the sketchpad' to 1.
If 'the sketchpad' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-11: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad'.

--- BAS-12, 13: comment spanning lines and nested parens ---
a number called cupboard is 0.
(nothing unusual here, just the dispatch note
double-checked against outgoing post)
Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.
(((a note about cupboard)))
Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.
If cupboard is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-12: expected 2 got {cupboard}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.

--- BAS-14: parens inside a string literal ---
a text called workbench is "the (a note about cupboard) reads fine".
a buffer called storeroom is workbench.
If storeroom's size is not 38 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-14: expected 38 got {storeroom's size}", Exit 95. Print storeroom's size.

--- BAS-24: comment-only line does not close ---
a number called u1 is 0.
a number called 'the pigeonhole' is 0.
a number called 'the dispatch note' is 0.
a number called 'outgoing post' is 0.
While u1 is less than 4,
  Increment u1,
  If u1 is equal to 1 then, Set 'the dispatch note' to 'the dispatch note' add 1.
  (satchel, checked)
  Set 'the pigeonhole' to 'the pigeonhole' add 1.

Set 'outgoing post' to 'outgoing post' add 1.
If 'the pigeonhole' is not 4 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-24: expected 4 got {'the pigeonhole'}", Exit 95. Print 'the pigeonhole'.
If 'the dispatch note' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-24: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.
If 'outgoing post' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-24: expected 1 got {'outgoing post'}", Exit 95. Print 'outgoing post'.

--- BAS-16: blank line count invariant ---
a number called cupboard is 0.
Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.

Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.
If cupboard is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-16: expected 2 got {cupboard}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.

--- BAS-17: blank line closes a nested loop, Repeat ---
a number called cupboard is 0.
a number called workbench is 0.
a number called r1 is 0.
Repeat 2 times,
  Set r1 to r1 add 1,
  If r1 is equal to 1 then, Set cupboard to cupboard add 1.

Set workbench to workbench add 1.
If cupboard is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {cupboard}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.
If workbench is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {workbench}", Exit 95. Print workbench.

--- the same leaf, a seed that draws For each ---
a number called 'the dispatch note' is 0.
a number called 'the sketchpad' is 0.
For each number from 1 to 3,
  If number is equal to 1 then, Set 'the dispatch note' to 'the dispatch note' add 1.

Set 'the sketchpad' to 'the sketchpad' add 1.
If 'the dispatch note' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.
If 'the sketchpad' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad'.

--- the same leaf, a seed that draws While ---
a number called 'the register' is 0.
a number called 'the sketchpad' is 0.
a number called u2 is 0.
While u2 is less than 5,
  Increment u2,
  If u2 is equal to 1 then, Set 'the register' to 'the register' add 1.

Set 'the sketchpad' to 'the sketchpad' add 1.
If 'the register' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {'the register'}", Exit 95. Print 'the register'.
If 'the sketchpad' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-17: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad'.

--- BAS-41: blank line closes a loop and its enclosing function ---
a number called workbench is 0.
a number called storeroom is 0.
To cupboard.
    a number called u3 is 0.
    While u3 is less than 4,
        Increment u3,
        If u3 is equal to 1 then, Set workbench to workbench add 1.

cupboard.
Set storeroom to storeroom add 1.
If workbench is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-41: expected 1 got {workbench}", Exit 95. Print workbench.
If storeroom is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-41: expected 1 got {storeroom}", Exit 95. Print storeroom.

--- BAS-43: blank line closes an On error block ---
a buffer called b1 is 20 bytes in size.
a number called workbench is 0.
a number called storeroom is 0.
a number called toolbox is 0.
Print byte 38 of b1.
On error
  Set workbench to workbench add 1,
  If workbench is equal to 1 then, Set storeroom to storeroom add 1.

Set toolbox to toolbox add 1.
If workbench is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-43: expected 1 got {workbench}", Exit 95. Print workbench.
If storeroom is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-43: expected 1 got {storeroom}", Exit 95. Print storeroom.
If toolbox is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-43: expected 1 got {toolbox}", Exit 95. Print toolbox.

--- BAS-46: blank line after a comma is cosmetic ---
a number called u4 is 0.
a number called 'the pigeonhole' is 0.
a number called 'the dispatch note' is 0.
While u4 is less than 4,
  Set 'the pigeonhole' to 'the pigeonhole' add 1,

  Increment u4.
Set 'the dispatch note' to 'the dispatch note' add 1.
If 'the pigeonhole' is not 4 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-46: expected 4 got {'the pigeonhole'}", Exit 95. Print 'the pigeonhole'.
If 'the dispatch note' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BAS-46: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.

